SelfSurge discovers plugins from Kelee's catalog, fmz200's split Surge modules,
and ddgksf2013's AdBlock rewrites. sources.json records selected sources,
source checksums, alternatives, exclusions, and resource provenance.

Selection groups app names and filename aliases, preferring body/script
cleanup, then URL rewrites, then domain rules. Ties prefer Kelee, fmz200,
then ddgksf2013. This is a deterministic coverage heuristic, not a guarantee
of runtime effectiveness. Domain-only fmz200 fragments and explicitly retired
plugins are omitted from the individual catalog. Existing module filenames
are retained; duplicate legacy URLs remain as aliases outside the web catalog.

Kelee modules are adaptations of Loon templates from https://hub.kelee.one/
and retain supplied author metadata and source URLs. They are distributed for
non-commercial use under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

fmz200 modules come from https://github.com/fmz200/wool_scripts. SelfSurge
normalizes metadata, script identifiers, jq syntax, and dependency URLs.
The upstream GPL-3.0 license is included at
resources/licenses/fmz200-wool_scripts-LICENSE.

YouTube_remove_ads.sgmodule and its mirrored scripts come from Maasea's
Apache-2.0-licensed native Surge module. SelfSurge adds category metadata and
replaces its script URLs with local mirrors. The upstream license is mirrored
at resources/licenses/Maasea-sgmodule-LICENSE.

ddgksf2013 app modules are adapted from
https://github.com/ddgksf2013/Rewrite/tree/master/AdBlock.
StartUpAds.sgmodule is adapted from the standalone Quantumult X rewrite at
https://ddgksf2013.top/rewrite/StartUpAds.conf (fetched with User-Agent: surge).
It retains full general coverage by default and can be used alongside app
modules. Select enabled apps in the web catalog and paste the resulting value
into the general module's exclude_apps parameter. Matching app rules are then
disabled by Surge line requirements; other general rules remain enabled.
Exclusions use app aliases, exact patterns, and unambiguous service hosts.
Shared service hosts alone do not establish app ownership. The parameter is
manual: it does not read Surge's enabled-module state. This feature requires
Core 22 (Surge iOS 5.11 / Mac 5.7) or later. Non-ad routing and
TestFlight/membership tweaks are excluded. Upstream terms and attribution
remain applicable; SelfSurge does not relicense these sources.

Files under scripts/ and resources/ are unmodified mirrors except for
scripts/adapted/: these retain upstream scripts inside a small adapter for
Quantumult X status strings and mock responses. sources.json records the
transformation and both original and adapted checksums. Copyright and license
terms remain with the respective upstream authors.

Script-Hub was studied as a behavioral reference. Its GPL-3.0 source code was
not copied into SelfSurge.
